{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgieYvjUPPosN6BFmXgd1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Today (Wed 4 Nov) the three cities are very close. Gdańsk comes out slightly ahead because it's the mildest and has the cleanest air.\n\n| | Warsaw | Gdańsk | Wrocław |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Temperature | 4 – 9.5 °C | **6.6 – 10.6 °C** | 6.2 – 9.8 °C |\n| Feels like | 1.7 – 6.9 °C | **4.1 – 7.5 °C** | 3 – 6.4 °C |\n| Sky | Overcast | Light rain | Light rain |\n| Rain | 17%, 0 mm | 25%, 0.1 mm | **13%, 0 mm** |\n| Wind / gusts | 12.6 / 28 km/h | **10.4 / 25 km/h** | 11.2 / 27 km/h |\n| Air quality (EAQI) | 67 – poor | **49 – moderate** | 53 – moderate |\n| Sunset | 16:01 | 16:04 | **16:21** |\n\n**Gdańsk is the nicest.** It's the warmest of the three, including the \"feels like\" temperature, it has the lightest wind and its air is the cleanest. The only downside is a chance of light drizzle, but the forecast total is just 0.1 mm.\n\n**Wrocław is a close second.** It has the lowest rain chance and about 20 minutes more daylight than the other two, but it feels a little colder.\n\n**Warsaw is the least pleasant.** It has the coldest morning (feels like about 2 °C) and its air quality is rated poor, so hard outdoor exercise isn't advised there today.\n\nNone of them need an umbrella. In all three cities you'll want a warm jacket and a sweater."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1599,"cache_read_input_tokens":42834,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1599},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"db62aa00-ad91-40cf-a3d8-bab7682c5c58","uuid":"d41a3ece-45c2-4d50-913f-006a74913245","timestamp":"2026-11-04T22:06:46.24